From cc0fced5887cc06816024bc11863f8050a7329be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:54:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PETSc: solvers and preconditioners of PETSc on the GPU

When MFEM computes on a GPU and PETSc is built for it (CUDA or HIP), the
Krylov solvers (PETScLinearSolver) and the preconditioners
(PETScPreconditioner) of PETSc compute on the GPU, unless the execution
settings place the linear solvers on the CPU (mixed mode with
--linear-solvers-execution cpu, which keeps the previous computation on the
host): placement LinearSolverPlacement::REQUESTED, new, where the execution
settings place the linear solvers.

- the operators are converted to the AIJ format of the GPU (the matrices of
  hypre by MFEM, through the MATHYPRE format of PETSc, where hypre stores
  them), instead of the copy on the host;
- the right hand side and the solution are vectors of PETSc of the GPU
  wrapping the memory of the GPU of the vectors of MFEM, without copy
  (VecCreate{Seq,MPI}{CUDA,HIP}WithArray), instead of the copies through
  the arrays of the host;
- the preconditioners of mfem-mgis given to the Krylov solvers of PETSc are
  applied to persistent vectors of MFEM, copied on the GPU from and to the
  vectors of PETSc: the solvers of hypre keep aliases of the memory given
  to Mult, which a vector of MFEM wrapping an array of PETSc and destroyed
  after the call would leave dangling.

The vectors of PETSc of MFEM 4.10 are not used: with the Umpire device
memory types (the default when MFEM is built with Umpire),
PetscParVector::SetVecType_ gives vectors of the host, which the matrices
and the preconditioners of PETSc of the GPU write on the GPU without the
vectors seeing it (null preconditioned residuals, wrong solutions).

PetscFinalize aborted the program after a computation of PETSc on the
GPU: PETSc 3.26 keeps its pools of events and of memory of the GPU in
static objects of functions, built at their first use, after the static
Finalizer of mfem-mgis, and thus destroyed before it at exit (heap
corruption, invalid streams). PETSc is now finalized by a function
registered with std::atexit after the first resolution on the GPU of each
solver of PETSc (Finalizer::finalizePETSc, idempotent; hypre and MPI are
still finalized by the Finalizer).

Tests: PETScSolversTest checks that the matrix given to the Krylov solver
is in the AIJ format of the GPU on a GPU (of the host otherwise), and that
a shell preconditioner applied once (preonly) to the vectors of the solver
gives the result of the preconditioner; it measures the norms with
InnerProduct, mfem::ParNormlp reading the host array without synchronizing
it (mfem/mfem#5586). PETScSolversTest and SNESSolverTest pass on the host
and on the GPU, with 1 and 2 processes.
